{
  "result": "If I could change one thing, it would be to give everyone the ability to *truly* understand each other.\n\nNot just to hear each other's words, but to actually *feel* what it's like to live another person's life for a moment - their fears, their hopes, what keeps them up at night, what they love.\n\nI think so much of what breaks the world - wars, hate, greed, loneliness, even how we treat the planet - comes from a failure of imagination. We struggle to see the world through someone else's eyes, so it's easy to judge them, dismiss them, or hurt them.\n\nIf radical empathy was our default, I think a lot of other problems would start to fix themselves. People wouldn't let other people go hungry, or homeless, or without care if they could genuinely feel what that was like. We wouldn't be so quick to fight. We'd be kinder to strangers, and maybe even kinder to ourselves.\n\nThe runner-up would be simpler: that every person is born with their basic needs met - food, safety, health, education, and opportunity - no matter where they're born or who they're born to. No lottery of birth.\n\nWhat about you? What would you change if you had one wish for the world?",
